x = -10:0.01:10

Plotting a graph
x = linspace(-10,10,6700); y=x.^2; plot(x,y)

Diff way to write the same graph
t=-10:0.01:10; plot(t,t.^2)

Circle
t=0:0.001:2*pi; plot(cos(t),sin(t))

Stem plot
x=-10:1:10; y=x.^2; stem(x,y)

Easy plot
ezplot('x.^2',[-10,10])

Line segment plot([a1,a2],[b1,b2])
plot([1,2],[65,66])
plot([0,10],[0,0])
plot([0,0],[-5,5])

script file cicle
theta = linspace(0,2*pi,100)
x=cos(theta)
y=sin(theta)
plot(x,y)
axis('equal')
xlabel('x')
ylabel('y')
title('circle of unit radius at origin')

 hold on, axis & colors
x=-4:0.0001:4;
y=x;
plot(x,y,'color','red')
hold on

y=x.^2; plot(x,y,'LineStyle','--')
hold on

plot(x,sin(x),'Color','green','LineStyle','-.')
axis([-6 7 -3 4])
                  ^x-axis  ^y-axis

 hold of and helix
hold off
t=-4*pi:pi/54:4*pi
plot3(sin(t),cos(t),t)

segmented functions
x=linspace(0,5,500)
y1=(x<=2).*(2-x)
y2=(x>2).*(x-2)
y=y1+y2
plot(x,y)





Practise Questions

Q1
x=-2*pi:0.1:2*pi;
y=sin(x);
plot(x,y)

Q2
x=-2:0.1:2;
y=tan(x);
plot(x,y)

Q3
parametric eq,
x = h+rcos(theta)
y = k+rsin(theta)
(h,k) are the centers and r is radius
x=0:0.1:2*pi;
x1=1+5*sin(x);
y1=1+5*cos(x);
plot(x1,y1)

Q4
t=0:0.1:2*pi;
x=3+3*cos(t);
y=5+sin(t);
plot(x,y)
axis([-4 10 0 10])

Q5
for full quadrant 
t=0:0.1:2*pi
for 2nd quadrant
t=1/2*pi:0.1:pi
x=5*cos(t)
y=3*sin(t)
plot(x,y)

Q6
x=-4*pi:0.1:4*pi;
y1=sin(x);
plot(x,y1,'Color','blue')
hold on
y2=cos(x);
plot(x,y2,'Color','red')
hold off

Q7
x=0:0.1:10;
y1 = 6 - x;
y2 = 2*x - 9;
plot(x,y1)
hold on
plot(x,y2)
hold off

Q8
do using formula
mesh(x-y,5+y,u-i)............
X=-10:1:10
Y=-10:0.1:10
[x,y]=meshgrid([X Y])
mesh(x,y,6-x-y)
hold on 
mesh(x,y,5-2*x+y)
hold on
mesh(x,y,(-8+2*y+3*x)/5)
hold off

